    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14561#issuecomment-6064860942\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14561\">PR #14561</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Looks like freebsd failed to build where the pinned version of <code>mio</code> doesn't build with the updated version of <code>libc</code> -- perhps fixed by a mio update?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 630207534,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791478535
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>auronandace <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14561#issuecomment-6079608446\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14561\">PR #14561</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Can confirm, <code>mio</code> 1.2.4 fixes the freebsd issue with <code>libc</code> 0.2.190: <a href=\"https://github.com/tokio-rs/mio/pull/2016\">https://github.com/tokio-rs/mio/pull/2016</a></p>\n<p>Do you need me to update the dependencie in this PR or should that be a maintainer job? I'm guessing that will need vetting too.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 630392276,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791543853
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>bjorn3 <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14561#issuecomment-6079722902\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14561\">PR #14561</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I believe there is going to be another libc release soon adding back the removed const as <code>#[deprecated]</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 630394056,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791544330
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>pchickey <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14561#issuecomment-6085669610\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14561\">PR #14561</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>@auronandace We'll make it your responsibility for Cargo.lock to have the correct deps in it that pass on all platforms, and then we will add whatever vets are required.</p>\n<p>You can put the magic string \"prtest:full\" into a commit message so that the full test matrix runs on the PR, not just when it enters the merge queue. That should demonstrate that the freebsd failure is fixed and just vets are required to proceed.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 630484064,
